  "notes": "{継|つ}ぐ means to succeed or take over something from a predecessor.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {家業|かぎょう}を{継|つ}ぐ: to take over the family business\n- {後|あと}を{継|つ}ぐ: to succeed someone\n- {跡|あと}を{継|つ}ぐ: to inherit a position/legacy\n- {王位|おうい}を{継|つ}ぐ: to succeed to the throne\n\nKANJI DISTINCTION:\n- {継|つ}ぐ: to succeed, inherit\n- {注|つ}ぐ: to pour (liquid)\n- {接|つ}ぐ: to join, graft, splice\n- {次|つ}ぐ: to rank next to\n\nRELATED:\n- {後継者|こうけいしゃ}: successor\n- {継承|けいしょう}: succession, inheritance",
